Name the commit a scanner number was read off

A pass measured PR 3197 with `--bar 69a4572b9...HEAD` while HEAD was at
7f7094f62, then wrote the result up as the range 69a4572b9...36b7f857d.
Both commits are real and both readings are real -- 1515/1233 and
1517/1235 -- but the one in the write-up was never measured, and the
handoff built on it carried a number nobody could reproduce. It survived
every check downstream because the number was right.

quality-pipeline.md already had the rule and scoped it to one carrier:
"a spawn prompt describes the tree you read, never the tree you
intended". A handoff is not a spawn prompt, and neither is a report to a
human, which is how this one travelled. Widened in place rather than
given a second home.

